WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.480
Futurama is undoubtedly one of the&nbsp;
greatest sci-fi comedies of all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.400
time — but despite its surprisingly&nbsp;
tight and well thought-out timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.520
the series didn't answer every question it&nbsp;
raised. For example, what became of Bender's son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.600
Ben? What happens to Fry and Leela after&nbsp;
the time-bending events of the finale?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.640
Is Fry's old girlfriend, Michelle, still going&nbsp;
out with the reanimated body of Pauly Shore?

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.840
"'Tis better to have loved and&nbsp;
lost, n'est pas? Ngngyyahagah!"

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.520
The answers to all of these questions&nbsp;
could make for intriguing episodes;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.600
ones we'll likely never get to see. And while&nbsp;
we can all live with a little mystery in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.640
year 3000, there's one lingering question, in&nbsp;
particular, that stands out as particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.840
irksome. What is the Other, and why is&nbsp;
she so important to the universe's future?

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:51.040
We know who the Other is, of course. It's Leela.&nbsp;
That's revealed in the season four episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:56.080
The Why of Fry, which is arguably one of the&nbsp;
most important Futurama episodes ever made.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.080
In it, Fry learns that the accident that landed&nbsp;
him in the cryogenic [kry-oh-JEN-ick] freezing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.000
tube and sent him to the future&nbsp;
wasn't actually an accident at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:09.280
It was part of a scheme by Nibbler, who spills&nbsp;
Futurama's big secret during the episode:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:15.040
Fry isn't just a doofus. He's actually the&nbsp;
most important person in the entire universe.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.000
See, because Fry is his own grandfather, the&nbsp;
former pizza delivery boy is immune to attacks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.520
by the evil Brainspawn, making him the only person&nbsp;
who can stop their plans for galactic genocide.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.400
In The Why of Fry, the Nibblonians give&nbsp;
Fry a Quantum Interphase Bomb and send&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.640
him off to fight the Brainspawn, where he&nbsp;
defeats them and saves the entire galaxy.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.600
"Here we are, trapped for eternity."

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:39.520
"We could sing 'American Pie.'"

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.320
Unfortunately, there's a complication, as tends&nbsp;
to be the case with anything involving the Planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:50.160
Express crew, and Fry ends up back in 1999,&nbsp;
before he was frozen and sent to the future.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:55.040
After some time-travel shenanigans, Fry goes back&nbsp;
to that fateful moment when he became stuck in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.040 --> 00:02:00.480
the cryogenic unit. It may seem like a retcon,&nbsp;
but if you go back to watch the Futurama pilot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.360
you'll see Nibbler's shadow&nbsp;
underneath where Fry sat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.760
showing how the creative team behind the&nbsp;
sitcom had their plan in place all along.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:13.440
Back to Season 4, and Fry tries to stop Nibbler&nbsp;
from sending his original body to the year 3000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.280
Nibbler protests, however, arguing that&nbsp;
there must be something in the future that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.680
Fry thinks is worth saving. That's where&nbsp;
the crucial piece of dialogue comes in.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.240
"She must be the other."

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.560
"The wha?"

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:28.080
"You must not give up on her."

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:33.040
Fry doesn't know what that means… and we don't,&nbsp;
either. Sadly, it seems like we never will.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.080
Fox canceled Futurama after its fourth season,&nbsp;
and while it came back from the dead two times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:41.360
the writers never bothered to explain&nbsp;
what Nibbler was talking about.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:46.000
Given The Why of Fry's important place in&nbsp;
Futurama canon, Nibbler's words seem like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.640
they carry a lot of weight — or they would,&nbsp;
if they were ever elaborated on. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.720
in the absence of a real explanation,&nbsp;
fans have concocted their own theories.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.760
Many assume that the Nibblonians have plans for&nbsp;
Leela that never made it to the screen. Meanwhile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.640
some think that Nibbler simply meant that Leela is&nbsp;
the second-most important person in the universe.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:10.000
As that theory goes, Leela essentially saved&nbsp;
the galaxy by making Fry care. Ultimately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.600
Fry decides to send his past self to the future&nbsp;
in The Why of Fry because he loves Leela. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.560
she's indirectly responsible for all of Fry's&nbsp;
heroics. Fry is the one in the middle of things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.600
but Leela is the person who&nbsp;
gives Fry something to fight for.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:27.920
Other fans suggest that Nibbler might be&nbsp;
referring to the series finale, in which Fry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.160
and Leela live together as a couple for decades&nbsp;
while everyone else around them is stuck in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:36.560
time. Maybe it's even a Star Wars reference&nbsp;
— Nibbler and Yoda have some similarities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.040
after all, although you've gotta hope that Fry&nbsp;
and Leela aren't secretly brother and sister.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.640
Whatever the case, fan theories&nbsp;
are the only explanations as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.240
the Other's significance that we're&nbsp;
going to get. By all indications,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:53.360
Futurama isn't ever coming back — making this&nbsp;
one big question that's bound to go unanswered.

